{"mappings":[{"caseId":"HEART-004","rationale":"The all, latest and skip subtests evaluate at base+35 with a 10-second recurrence and MaxBatch=2. All asserts two work occurrences after one evaluation and four after a second at the same time, supporting bounded batches and retained backlog. Latest asserts nominal=base+30 and covered_count=4. Skip asserts one skipped work occurrence. Limits: skip does not check which nominal instants are recorded as omitted; all does not inspect individual identities or coverage; no actual downtime/restart is exercised. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestCatchUp"},{"caseId":"HEART-006","rationale":"The test attempts and acknowledges an occurrence, closes and reopens the store, and checks that serialized status contains acknowledged and contains no verified state. Evaluating at base+21 must create exactly one return-review occurrence, supporting preservation of unresolved acknowledgement and a return watch across restart. Limits: acknowledgement is invoked directly without transport; status is checked by string matching; the test does not directly inspect the persisted deadline or assert an explicit possibly-executed classification. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestUncertainEffectAndRestartQuestions"},{"caseId":"HEART-001","rationale":"With coverage ending at base+100 and planning review scheduled at base+70, evaluation at base+70 must create exactly one planning-review occurrence. Renewal at base+71 supplies a plan digest and extends coverage to base+200 and review to base+150. Evaluation at base+101 must produce no fallback, and a database query asserts both updated timestamps. This supports review creation before expiry and effective renewal beyond the original coverage boundary. Limits: no restart or crash tests durability or atomicity; the test does not evaluate at the new review deadline or inspect next-period work publication. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestPlanningRollover"},{"caseId":"HEART-005","rationale":"The allow, defer and coalesce subtests attempt and acknowledge the first occurrence, then evaluate the next nominal instant at base+10. Attempting the next occurrence must succeed for allow and fail for defer and coalesce while the first remains unresolved. After a verified report with an evidence digest for the first occurrence, the blocked attempt must succeed. This supports policy-dependent publication gating without treating acknowledgement as completion. Limits: attempts and acknowledgement are direct store calls, not transport delivery; the test does not assert coalesced coverage or omission records, validate the evidence independently, or exercise restart durability. This is source-level evidence, not an observed test pass.","testName":"TestOverlap"}]}
